.TH EXAMPLE\-SENDER\-C 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-bigredbox 2.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
example\-sender\-c \- send a Mu2e DAQ alert using the C library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B example\-sender\-c
[\fB\-s\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-i\fR \fIADDRESS\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fINUM\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B example\-sender\-c
constructs a JSON alert payload and broadcasts it as a single UDP datagram.
It is a minimal demonstration of the
.B libdaq_alert
C library interface.
.PP
The payload format is:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
{"system_id":"...","timestamp":"<ISO\-8601>","message":"..."}
.fi
.RE
.PP
The timestamp is generated automatically at the time of the call.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-system\-id " " \fIID\fR
Identifier of the sending system.
.br
Default: \fBDAQ\-NODE\-01\fR
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-message " " \fITEXT\fR
Human\-readable alert message.
.br
Default: \fBTest alert from example\-sender\-c\fR
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ip " " \fIADDRESS\fR
UDP destination address: a dotted\-quad IPv4 broadcast or unicast address.
.br
Default: \fB255.255.255.255\fR
.br
Anything that is not a dotted quad, including a host name, is silently sent
to 255.255.255.255 and reported as success (see
.BR libdaq_alert (3)).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fINUM\fR
UDP destination port (1\(en65535).
.br
Default: \fB37020\fR
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Alert sent successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid port, unknown option, field longer than 2041 bytes, or a socket
error.
An unparseable
.B \-\-ip
is not detected.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send an alert with default parameters:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
example\-sender\-c
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send an alert to a specific subnet with a custom system ID and message:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
example\-sender\-c \-\-system\-id DAQ\-NODE\-03 \e
    \-\-message "Readout buffer overflow" \e
    \-\-ip 192.168.1.255
.fi
.RE
.SH BUILDING
Build and install from the
.I libs/
directory of the repository:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
cmake \-B build \-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=./install
cmake \-\-build build
cmake \-\-install build
.fi
.RE
.PP
The installed binary is placed in
.IR <prefix>/bin/example\-sender\-c .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libdaq_alert (3),
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-api (7),
.BR example\-sender\-cpp (1),
.BR example\-sender\-py (1)
